# Every build tree. There are several by necessity, not by accident: gpumem must
# be configured against the NVHPC toolchain in its own dir (build-gpumem), and
# tools/build_all.sh drives per-configuration trees under build-all/. Matches
# the --exclude 'build-*' that tests/hpc/run_on_mn5.sh has always used.
build/
build-*/
.cache/
compile_commands.json
pcomm-out/

# Your global ignore (~/.config/git/ignore) has PLAN-*.md; plans/ is a tracked
# part of this repo on purpose — a plan that only exists on disk is exactly the
# thing plans/ exists to prevent. Repo .gitignore outranks the global excludes.
!plans/PLAN-*.md

# Locally built flatc (tools/get_flatc.sh) — arch-specific, not committed.
.tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-machine tool settings. Ignored here rather than only in a developer's
# ~/.config/git/ignore, because the MN5 clone has no such global file and would
# otherwise report it as untracked on every suite sync.
.claude/

# Upstream sources kept locally for reading, never for building or vendoring:
# NVSHMEM and NCCL. Several questions this project has answered the expensive
# way — which door creates a queue pair, how a dmabuf fd is obtained — are one
# grep away in their source. Ignored because they are large, arch-independent
# and belong to their upstreams; anything we actually depend on gets vendored
# under third_party/ with its licence, as mlx5 is.
reference/

# Upstream checkouts kept for working against rather than for reading: spack,
# under references/spack. The package recipe we maintain is tracked, under
# spack_repo/ — this is only the clone it gets registered with, which belongs to
# its own upstream and carries its own .git. Plural, and distinct from the
# reference/ above, which is read-only source.
references/

# PNG renders of demos/figures/*.svg. The SVGs are the source and are tracked;
# the slides reference them by .svg name. These are ad-hoc renders made to show
# a figure on a projector — 1.5 MB of derived pixels with no script to
# regenerate them from, which is the wrong thing to carry in history.
demos/figures/*.png
